            <ArticleTitle>Nifedipine--a survey of adverse effects. Four years' reporting in Sweden.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>133-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>During the period February 1983 to December 1984 the Swedish Adverse Drug Reactions Advisory Committee received 80 reports describing 116 adverse reactions with a possible or probable connection to nifedipine. The most frequently reported reactions are oedema, tachycardia, headache and rash. Confusion and sleep disorders constitute 8 cases. Impaired angina is a potentially serious reaction and one patient developed myocardial infarction.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
